{
  // `@luke/core` is an ESM package: `package.json` declares `"type": "module"`,
  // so `module: NodeNext` emits ESM and every relative import in `src/` must
  // carry an explicit `.js` extension — Node's ESM resolver does no extension
  // guessing. Dropping those extensions fails the build; do not "tidy" them.
  //
  // ESM-only rather than dual: the browser is a real consumer (`apps/web` ships
  // core to the client, and the Vitest browser tier loads `dist` directly), and
  // a CommonJS artifact cannot serve named ESM imports there. The CommonJS
  // consumers — `apps/api` and `packages/calendar`, both of which emit
  // `require("@luke/core")` — reach it through Node's `require(esm)`, supported
  // unflagged on the Node 24 this repo pins everywhere. That works only while
  // the graph stays free of top-level `await`, which would make the package
  // unloadable from `require()` (`ERR_REQUIRE_ASYNC_MODULE`).
  //
  // `DOM` on top of the base's neutral `lib` is this package's one deliberate
  // exception, and it is narrow: `crypto/secrets.server.ts` and `runtime/env.ts`
  // hold three `typeof window` guards that are the whole point of an isomorphic
  // package — they decide which side they are running on. Without `DOM` those
  // three lines fail with TS2304, measured. What is *not* inherited any more is
  // the rest of `lib.es2022.full`: DOM.Iterable, DOM.AsyncIterable, ScriptHost
  // and WebWorker.ImportScripts, none of which this package uses.
  //
  // `types: ["node"]` stays even though core ships to the browser: `types` has
  // no per-file granularity, and the per-file runtime split is enforced by the
  // per-runtime ESLint globals instead (see `eslint.config.mjs`).
  //
  // No `composite` and no `incremental`: no project references this one, and
  // an incremental build trusts `tsconfig.tsbuildinfo` over the filesystem —
  // after `rm -rf dist` it reported success and emitted nothing. A plain `tsc`
  // always emits every output, so `build` can delete `dist` first.
  "extends": "../../tsconfig.base.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "module": "NodeNext",
    "moduleResolution": "NodeNext",
    "lib": ["ES2022", "DOM"],
    "outDir": "./dist",
    "rootDir": "./src",
    "declaration": true,
    "declarationMap": true,
    "sourceMap": true,
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*"],
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules",
    "dist",
    "src/**/__tests__/**",
    "**/*.test.ts",
    "**/*.spec.ts"
  ]
}
